Q - a blessed scroll of John H.:
> Moving Clouds (makes the clouds on the Plane of Air move like the water
> bubbles do on the Plane of Water)
>
This reminded me of a sequence of Dudley strips:
   http://www.nicolaas.net/dudley/archive.php?f=20040817
which always struck me as a fun YANI!

> AoY Container (makes identification possibly useful even if all major
> item classes are ID'd, by removing the major ways of differentiating
> the Amulet from an imitation without it)
>
If you're dropping the distinction between which can be put into a
container, I'd vote in favour of plastic ones being too large to fit
also, rather than the other way around. It'd take more code for the
Wizard and other covetous monsters to figure out what to steal. This
raises the interesting question; would Rodney be fooled by a plastic
Amulet long enough for him to grab it and 'port away? Could be a
convenient hold-off technique; drop a plastic AoY and then leg it to
the upstairs!

> Assorted YAFM's (Specifically, for the message if you win while
> hallucinating.)
>
